  "metaDescription": "President Prabowo Subianto and legislative leaders discuss selecting a new Vice President following the resignation of Gibran Rakabuming Raka.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "President Prabowo Subianto is holding meetings with coalition parties and legislative leadership to determine a successor for the vacant vice presidency.",
    "The People's Consultative Assembly aims to finalize the appointment process for the new vice president by December 4.",
    "Political parties have varying positions on the vacancy, with the Democratic Party declining to submit candidates while others discuss potential nominees."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian government is currently managing the transition of the vice-presidential office following the resignation of Gibran Rakabuming Raka. President Prabowo Subianto has initiated consultations with the leadership of the People's Consultative Assembly and the House of Representatives to facilitate the selection process. While coalition parties are being gathered to discuss candidates, responses from political organizations remain mixed; for instance, the Democratic Party has publicly stated it will not propose any names for the position, opting to defer the decision to the President. Meanwhile, legislative officials are working to establish a timeline for the formal appointment, with a current goal to complete the process by early December. Media attention has focused on the procedural steps for the parliamentary plenary session that will eventually confirm the new official.",
